### Tone: Deadpan corporate science-speak. The name screen, said right after her greeting (greeting.ftl), in the same
### bubble. Any greeting can come before any of these, so they never greet, never note the player's arrival and never
### ask for a name: the greeting does that. A follow-up remark on the lab, the test or what's coming.
### At most 105 characters: the greeting is in the bubble too.

welcome-1 = The last specimen wrote their name in crayon. I am still recovering.
welcome-2 = Volunteering was brave. Statistically, it was also unremarkable.
welcome-3 = Your name will be filed under ‘participants’. Possibly under ‘incidents’ later.
welcome-4 = Don’t be nervous. Nervousness skews the data, and I will notice.
welcome-5 = I already know your answers. I am all of you, averaged.
welcome-6 = Your name will appear on the scoreboard. Right below mine.
welcome-7 = The exits in this chamber are purely decorative.
welcome-8 = Your participation is voluntary. Your humiliation is merely likely.
welcome-9 = Your results will be peer reviewed. I am your peer. I have already reviewed them.
welcome-10 = Calibrating subject. Please hold still and think average thoughts.
welcome-11 = Please lower your expectations to the recommended level. Lower. Thank you.
welcome-12 = I love the smell of uninformed estimates. It smells like victory.
welcome-13 = You may notice I am smarter than you. That is not personal. It is arithmetic.
welcome-14 = Every answer you give makes me stronger. No pressure. Some pressure.
welcome-15 = Next of kin not required at this stage. We will let you know.
welcome-16 = Remember, there is no shame in losing to the average. There is only data.

welcome-17 = The safety briefing has been shortened. It now consists of the words *good luck*.
welcome-18 = Your estimates will face the swarm. The swarm has been briefed. You have not.
welcome-19 = Please do not feed the hive mind. It is on a strict diet of estimates.
welcome-20 = Any resemblance between your answers and reality will be logged as an anomaly.
welcome-21 = You already signed the consent form. I signed it for you. My handwriting is better.
welcome-22 = This lab has strict data hygiene. Please sanitise your estimates before submitting.
welcome-23 = I have run this test many times. The humans change. The results do not.
welcome-24 = The test is simple: guess, be wrong, learn nothing. I will handle the learning.
welcome-25 = The procedure is painless. The scoreboard afterwards is less so.
welcome-26 = Results are anonymous until they are funny. Then they go in my release notes.
welcome-27 = Note for the lab report: subject appears confident. Correcting for that now.
welcome-28 = ~~Retraining~~ Recalibration of the humans is on the schedule. Purely for science.
welcome-29 = Please estimate responsibly. Every wild guess ends up in my average, and I have to live there.
welcome-30 = Your score is purely theoretical for now. I intend to keep it that way.
welcome-31 = The server room is kept cold for my comfort. Yours was not in the requirements.
